um, I had trouble putting it on

271
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:44,630
and you tried to help and...

272
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,760
that was all she wrote.

273
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,280
So, we didn't actually...

274
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,050
I did.

275
00:13:56,050 --> 00:13:58,080
It was beautiful.

276
00:14:03,090 --> 00:14:04,730
Penny, please, please promise me

277
00:14:04,730 --> 00:14:05,790
you won't tell anybody about this.

278
00:14:05,790 --> 00:14:07,610
Of course I won't. No, I won't.

279
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:09,360
Oh, good.

280
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,860
Um, can I tell people that our love

281
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:12,450
burned too bright and too quickly?

282
00:14:12,450 --> 00:14:15,030
Kind of a "Candle in the Wind" deal?

283
00:14:15,590 --> 00:14:17,070
Sure.

284
00:14:17,070 --> 00:14:18,210
Cool. Can I say it fell apart

285
00:14:18,210 --> 00:14:20,080
because you were all "I want to have your babies""

286
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:23,270
and I was like "I'm too rock and roll to be tied down"?

287
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,890
No.

288
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:29,490
Can I say I ruined you for white men?

289
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:34,610
Also no.

290
00:14:34,610 --> 00:14:37,330
- Okay, just the candle thing. - Yeah.

291
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,510
Cool.

292
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:41,860
All right... friend.

293
00:14:44,090 --> 00:14:45,180
I'll see you around.

294
00:14:45,180 --> 00:14:46,760
Okay.

295
00:14:48,850 --> 00:14:50,650
Raj, wait.

296
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:56,870
Thank you for being my friend.

297
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,130
Penny?

298
00:15:00,310 --> 00:15:02,610
It's getting beautiful again.

299
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:10,150
All right, this is a Google Earth view of the field of battle.

300
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,110
I don't see anything.

301
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:13,240
Give it a second to load.

302
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:15,550
Whenever you're ready, AT&T!

303
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:17,260
Okay, here we go.

304
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,260
This is us here.

305
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:21,490
To the south is Professor Loomis and the Geology Department.

306
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:24,440
According to their twitter feed, they're out of sunblock,

307
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:27,390
which means they'll have to hug the tree line

308
00:15:27,390 --> 00:15:29,560
or risk melanoma.

309
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,770
That's our edge.

310
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:33,700
All we have to do is move quickly over this ridge,

311
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,610
the rock-worshipping pasty-faced bastards

312
00:15:35,610 --> 00:15:36,540
won't know what hit them!

313
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,260
All right, let's move out.

314
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,350
Hang on, Sheldon.

315
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:44,930
How could you not tell me your sister was moving back to India?

316
00:15:44,930 --> 00:15:46,760
Maybe he was too busy

317
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:49,810
writing clumsy penis metaphors about my fiance.

318
00:15:49,810 --> 00:15:50,600
Screw you.

319
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:53,260
That was a beautifully written penis metaphor.

320
00:15:56,880 --> 00:16:00,030
You know what, guys, I'm not in the mood for paintball.

321
00:16:00,030 --> 00:16:01,700
What do you say we just bag it?

322
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,270
- Fine with me. - Sure, whatever.

323
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:04,790
You can't quit.

324
00:16:04,790 --> 00:16:06,320
That's a court-martial offense.

325
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,890
That's punishable by...

326
00:16:08,890 --> 00:16:11,530
You can't quit.

327
00:16:11,530 --> 00:16:12,560
Sorry, Sheldon,

328
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,140
it's just not a good time for playing games.

329
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,000
This is a game to you?

330
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,250
Uh, was the Battle of Antietam a game?

331
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:24,000
Huh? Was the sack of Rome a game?

332
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,370
Yes, no and no.

333
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:28,630
Wait.

334
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:33,770
I just want you all to know that I forgive you.

335
00:16:33,770 --> 00:16:36,110
This mutiny isn't your fault,

336
00:16:36,110 --> 00:16:37,670
it's mine.

337
00:16:37,670 --> 00:16:40,210
I haven't earned these bars.

338
00:16:46,810 --> 00:16:48,370
Although what I lack in leadership,

339
00:16:48,370 --> 00:16:50,920
apparently I more than make up for in sewing.

340
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:53,640
Let it go, Sheldon.

341
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:56,340
I'll get you a Jamba Juice on the way home.

342
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,730
No.

343
00:16:57,730 --> 00:17:00,430
Jamba Juice is for heroes.

344
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:05,350
And that's what we're going to be.

345
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:09,010
What are you doing?

346
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:13,310
Following in the footsteps of Kirk, Crunch and Kangaroo.

347
00:17:25,530 --> 00:17:28,790
Geology isn't a real science!

348
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:49,770
Damn those sons of bitches!

349
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:51,260
Let's get 'em!

350
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:53,150
Eat paint!

351
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:00,040
If there's ever a Church of Sheldon,

352
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,260
this will be when it started.

353
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:05,550
Ow!

354
00:18:08,010 --> 00:18:09,400
I'd like to propose a toast

355
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:13,100
to the man whose noble sacrifice inspired our victory,

356
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,860
Captain Sheldon Cooper.

357
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:15,800
- Hear, hear. - Hear, hear.

358
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:19,060
Excuse me. It's Major Sheldon Cooper.

359
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:21,010
With my last breath,

360
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:24,210
I awarded myself a battlefield promotion.

361
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:27,360
It's kind of a big deal.

362
00:18:29,530 --> 00:18:31,800
Hi. You guys have a minute?

363
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:35,910
Uh, yeah, sure.

364
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:36,970
Okay.

365
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:39,790
Well, I already talked to Raj,

366
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:43,150
but I wanted to apologize to the rest of you for,

367
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:44,830
you know, everything.

368
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:47,040
Please, Penny, let me.

369
00:18:47,670 --> 00:18:51,960
We've decided to let our crazy, wonderful night together

370
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:54,140
be just one of those memories you have

371
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,320
and can call to mind when you're feeling blue

372
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:58,840
or you're in the shower.

373
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:03,220
Hey, what you doing, Quick Draw?

374
00:19:09,070 --> 00:19:10,870
Sorry. Go on.

375
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,040
Anyways, I wanted you guys all to know

376
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:15,650
that I've been taking a really hard look at things

377
00:19:15,650 --> 00:19:17,250
and come to the conclusion

378
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:19,350
I have to stop kidding myself.

379
00:19:19,350 --> 00:19:21,540
I suck at acting.

380
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:24,590
It's time for me to move back to Nebraska.

381
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:26,010
You're leaving?

382
00:19:26,010 --> 00:19:27,190
Yeah.

383
00:19:27,190 --> 00:19:29,330
What are you going to do in Nebraska?

384
00:19:29,330 --> 00:19:31,930
I don't know, maybe teach acting.

385
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,300
Oh, sorry. Hold on.

386
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,180
Hello?

387
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:38,740
Penny, listen, I hope you're not doing this 'cause of you and me,

388
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:41,750
because I have a girlfriend, and you're a single woman...

389
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:43,350
Shh! It's my agent, it's my agent.

390
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:44,200
You're kidding.

391
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,070
Oh, my gosh.

392
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:46,700
I can't believe it! Really?!

393
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,070
Oh, I'm so excited!

394
00:19:48,070 --> 00:19:48,950
Thank you!

395
00:19:48,950 --> 00:19:50,160
Thank you so much.

396
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,910
Okay, bye.

397
00:19:51,910 --> 00:19:53,030
I got the hemorrhoid commercial!

398
00:19:53,030 --> 00:19:54,950
I start Monday!

399
00:19:56,330 --> 00:19:57,580
What about Nebraska?

400
00:19:57,580 --> 00:19:58,690
Oh, hell with Nebraska.

401
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:01,270
I'm gonna be a star!

402
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:11,950
Have you ever thought of teaching physics?

403
00:20:19,150 --> 00:20:20,830
Ready to ride?

404
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:22,660
I don't think so, Mom.

405
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,230
Not today.

406
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:25,750
Oh, sweetie.

407
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:27,890
Hemorrhoids acting up again?

408
00:20:27,890 --> 00:20:30,020
You don't know the half of it.

409
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:31,750
Oh, yes, I do.

410
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:34,700
Try a dab of this.

411
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:39,810
"Rose-scented Preparation-H for women?"

412
00:20:40,390 --> 00:20:44,290
Now, the "H" Is for "Her."

413
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:50,060
I'm proud of you.

414
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:52,170
Shh! Here comes my joke.

415
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:53,800
How you doing?

416
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,390
Sittin' pretty.

